# UI Component Standards

## Back Navigation — Always Use `BackToHubButton`

Any button that navigates back to the hub or a parent view MUST use `BackToHubButton`.
Never create a custom back button with `ArrowLeft` + inline Tailwind.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — custom back button
import { ArrowLeft } from 'lucide-react'
<button onClick={onBack} className="p-2 rounded-lg ...">
  <ArrowLeft className="w-5 h-5" />
</button>

// ✅ GOOD
import BackToHubButton from '@/components/ui/BackToHubButton'
<BackToHubButton onClick={onBack} />

// ✅ GOOD — custom label for non-hub destinations
<BackToHubButton onClick={onBack} label="Back to Inbox" />
```

`ArrowLeft` from lucide-react is only acceptable inside multi-step form wizard "Previous" buttons — not for page navigation.

---

## Cards — Always Use `Card` or `BlockCard`

Never use raw `<div>` with custom border/background/shadow classes as a card container.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 shadow-lg p-6">

// ✅ GOOD — general content card
import Card from '@/components/ui/Card'
<Card variant="elevated">

// ✅ GOOD — composable hub block
import BlockCard from '@/components/ui/BlockCard'
<BlockCard icon={ClipboardList} title="DOT Application" status="in-progress">
```

---

## Buttons — Always Use `Button`

Use the `Button` component for all interactive buttons. Inline button Tailwind is not allowed for primary/secondary/danger actions.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<button className="px-4 py-2 bg-teal-600 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-teal-500">

// ✅ GOOD
import Button from '@/components/ui/Button'
<Button variant="primary">Save</Button>
<Button variant="secondary">Cancel</Button>
<Button variant="danger" size="sm">Delete</Button>
<Button isLoading={saving}>Save</Button>
```

`ghost` variant is acceptable for icon-only utility buttons inside complex UI (e.g. modal close X).
